Problem: I keep putting off studying even though finals are close. I end up scrolling until midnight, feel guilty, and then sleep badly. I want to study consistently without panicking every night.
Relevant domains/subdomains: {"Behavioral": ["Routine", "Technology usage", "Productivity"], "Physical": ["Sleep"], "Psychological": ["Stress"]}

Generate interview questions, grounded in the domains above, that reveal patterns (not surface
facts) by exploring: what usually happens, when, what triggers it, what the user feels, what they
do afterward, what makes it better/worse, and recurring cycles.

